60818201338","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-qn.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-qn[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Scale the Admin Center Updates > Plugins sub-tab to 1000+ community[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]plugins[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The Updates tab's Plugins sub-tab loads, filters, and navigates a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]catalog of 1000+ community plugins without silent truncation, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]without a per-catalog-entry network storm, and with j/k [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]key-to-paint p95 under 16 ms.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]plugin_catalog_scale.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/plugin_catalog_scale.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-qn[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-qn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Large-catalog bench harness and recorded baselines[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]bench[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bench: add a slow-marked scale bench and large synthetic catalog fixture[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for the Updates > Plugins sub-tab, record p50/p95/max baselines at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]10/250/1000/2000 entries, and assert the fetch/enrich cost curves so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]later phases have a measuring stick.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Latest-version enrichment that scales with installed count, [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]not catalog size[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]enrich[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bench[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]enrich: remove the quadratic installed-version lookup, scope eager PyPI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enrichment to installed entries, add a lazy per-entry latest fetch for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the highlighted row, bound the fetch budget, and prune the unbounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]latest cache.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Catalog fetch past GitHub search's 1000-result cap[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]fetch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bench[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]fetch: shard the topic search so results above GitHub's hard 1000-item [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]search cap are still returned, surface truncation and incomplete_results[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]as catalog warnings, and make the gh timeout scale with page count [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of a flat 20 s.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Constant-time render, filter, and navigation paths[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bench[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui: batch OptionList population, replace the per-keystroke linear scans[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with identity maps built during rebuild, debounce the filter through the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing detail debouncer, precompute filter haystacks, and bound the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]incoming-commit caches.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Enforce the budgets and close out the epic[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bench, enrich, fetch, tui[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard: flip the recorded baselines into enforced budgets, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regression check alongside the other perf guards, verify the combined [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tree with check-full, and reconcile any feature flag opened during the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-qn","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-qn.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e2dd7015d76b74278c57a91272b1743d","started_at":"2026-08-19T00:14:01.692521+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-qn.land"]}
